VVEERRSSIIOONNSS
       When timer notifications are delivered via signals  (SSIIGGEEVV__SSIIGGNNAALL),  on
       Linux  it is also possible to obtain the overrun count via the _s_i___o_v_e_r_‐
       _r_u_n field of the _s_i_g_i_n_f_o___t structure (see ssiiggaaccttiioonn(2)).   This  allows
       an  application to avoid the overhead of making a system call to obtain
       the overrun count, but is a nonportable extension to POSIX.1.

       POSIX.1 discusses timer overruns only in the context of timer notifica‐
       tions using signals.

